OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,AKing acknowledges 'suffering of the
OL,4,Apast' as Caribbean tour begins
OL,5,
OL,6,FPrior to the trip, Buckingham Palace
OL,7,Fsaid the King would not shy away from
OL,8,F"colonial legacy" and the impact of the
OL,9,Fslave trade during the visit but, in
OL,10,Fline with the UK government position,
OL,11,Fhe will not apologise for Britain's
OL,12,Frole in the slave trade or offer
OL,13,Freparations.
OL,15,FAppearing at his first engagement, he
OL,16,Ftold young people it is "only right" to
OL,17,F"acknowledge the great suffering and
OL,18,Finjustices of the past".
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/39
